  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=\u27e83{sec}^{2}\u2061(t),\\,-2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(t)\u27e9.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=\u27e82,\\,1\u27e9$ when $t=0,$ calculate the components of the the velocity vector of $P$ at time $t.$\n\n$v(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \u27e83{sec}^{2}\u2061(t),\\,-2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(t)\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e8\\int 3{sec}^{2}\u2061(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int -2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(t)\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(t)+{C}_{1},-2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(t)+{C}_{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=\u27e82,1\u27e9.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =\u27e83\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(0)+{C}_{1},-2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(0)+{C}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e82,1\u27e9 & =\u27e8{C}_{1},-2+{C}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & ={C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv(t)=\u27e83\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(t)+2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(t)+3\u27e9.\n$$",
